{title: 551 - Jesus, Savior, Pilot Me}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #551 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 551}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]Jesus, Savior, [Db/Ab]pilot [Eb7/Bb]me
[Db]Over life’s [Eb7]tempestuous [Ab]sea;
[Eb7]Unknown waves before [Ab]me [Eb7]roll,
[Eb7]Hiding rock and [Ab]treacherous shoal.
[Db/Ab]Chart and compass [Ab]come [Eb7/Bb]from Thee;
[Db]Jesus, Savior, [Eb7]pilot [Ab]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]As a mother [Db/Ab]stills [Ab]her [Eb7/Bb]child,
[Db]thou canst hush [Eb7]the ocean [Ab]wild;
[Eb7]boisterous waves obey thy will,
[Eb7]when thou sayest to [Ab]them, "Be still!"
[Db/Ab]Wondrous sovreign [Ab]of [Eb7/Bb]the sea,
[Db]Jesus, Savior, [Eb7]pilot [Ab]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]When at last [Db/Ab]I near [Ab]the [Eb7/Bb]shore,
[Db]and the fearful [Eb7]breakers [Ab]roar
[Eb7]'twixt me and the peaceful rest,
[Eb7]then, while leaning [Ab]on thy breast,
[Db/Ab]may I hear thee [Ab]say [Eb7/Bb]to me,
[Db]"Fear not, I [Eb7]will pilot [Ab]thee.
{end_of_verse}
